Subject: Serialize Function Bodies With Bounded Lazy-Ready Records

What this does
  Frames each serialized function body with an explicit checked length and
  parses the record through one bounded reader. The shared layout calculator
  validates alignment, counts, offsets, and allocation sizes before assigning
  any self-relative pointers.

Why we need it
  Function metadata can be read without consuming the body, while eager loading
  and later materialization use identical validation and pointer arithmetic.
  Hard body boundaries prevent malformed records from reading into following
  objects, and checked arithmetic protects 32-bit targets from wrapped layouts.

What it adds
  Length-prefixed function records, canonical body parsing, overflow-safe layout
  calculation, local-count validation, inline-cache and object-template checks,
  and the engine-owned source state needed by the later lazy reader. The reader
  remains copied-only in this patch; borrowed input and deferred atoms are added
  separately.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The function record layout changes and the complete series continues to
  use the authoritative BC_VERSION 28 bump in 9999-bc-version-bump.patch.

